-- a dependent eliminator (it takes a `motive`), so it is compiled where the `match` that uses it occurs: `Fun.ctorElim`
-- no type of the grammar describes it, and none can: `Fun.ctorIdx`: the parameter `x` of `Fun.ctorIdx` has type `Fun`, which the front end does not translate — every constructor of `Fun` takes a `Fun`, so the type has no values, and no `Ty` denotes an empty type
-- no type of the grammar describes it, and none can: `Fun.size`: the parameter `x.1` of `Fun.size` has type `Fun`, which the front end does not translate — every constructor of `Fun` takes a `Fun`, so the type has no values, and no `Ty` denotes an empty type
